From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:13:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] kk: MESA_KK_DUMP_MSL_MIN_KB dumps large pipelines' MSL
 and SPIR-V

A dev switch, off by default, to bring the shaders behind slow or failed
Metal builds off the phone. With MESA_KK_DUMP_MSL_MIN_KB=N, a Metal build
(render or compute) whose MSL is over N KB writes, before it is built, into
kk-dump beside MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR (on the phone Library/Caches/kk-dump,
which the app's container vends over AFC):

- MSL.STAGE.metal, each stage's MSL as Metal gets it;
- MSL.STAGE.spv, the SPIR-V of that stage of the pipeline being created,
  when its create info gives SPIR-V;
- MSL.txt last: kind, the full MSL hash, and per stage its MSL bytes and
  entry point, SPIR-V bytes and entry point and specialization constants
  (ID:hex bytes).

MSL is the first 16 hex digits of the MSL hash, as MESA_KK_DEBUG=compile's
msl= shows it; the hash is now taken once per build, before it. A hash
already dumped is not dumped again, and nothing more is written once the
directory holds 200 MB (logged once). Each dump logs
"[kk-dump] KIND msl=... bytes=...".

The Vulkan runtime remembers, per thread, the stage create infos of the
graphics or compute pipeline it is creating, and
vk_pipeline_creating_stage_spirv gives a stage's SPIR-V, entry point and
specialization from them; KosmicKrisp builds Metal pipelines within that
call, from translated or cached MSL alike.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-kk-msl-size.md
Offered-upstream: no
